WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:06.300
The SCP Foundation contains some of the most
dangerous objects and entities in the universe,

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:12.390
but there are a number of entries in the SCP
database that stretch the meaning of ‘containment’.

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:17.670
Containment is a principle value of the Foundation,
but let’s remember that this is an organization

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:23.260
that’s more than happy to bend even their
own rules if it better suits their needs.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:27.529
Just because it isn’t locked in a cell in
a high-security facility doesn’t mean that

00:00:27.529 --> 00:00:33.400
it’s not contained, but some anomalies are
too dangerous, too powerful, or simply too

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.640
far away to be given the standard “put it
in a box” treatment.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:43.410
And for some anomalies, maybe keeping them
out of the box is the best course of action.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:49.210
Such is the case of SCP-179, the entity known
as Sauelsuesor.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:54.980
For SCP-179, containment is focused around
the cover-up of its existence.

00:00:54.980 --> 00:01:00.160
Disinformation campaigns within institutions
that study the solar system and sabotage of

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:06.520
research regarding cis-Mercurian space, the
area within the moon’s orbit which SCP-179

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:11.560
is situated in, are the Foundation’s two
primary means of keeping this anomaly under

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:12.700
wraps.

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:17.799
After all, “40,000 km from the South polar
region of the solar photosphere” is pretty

00:01:17.799 --> 00:01:22.770
far, and even the Foundation would have difficulty
establishing traditional containment measures

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:24.279
with this anomaly.

00:01:24.279 --> 00:01:29.979
Though SCP-179’s distance may be beneficial,
as it’s not just outside of the Foundation’s

00:01:29.979 --> 00:01:35.549
reach, the lunar anomaly is kept free from
the prying hands of various Groups of Interest,

00:01:35.549 --> 00:01:40.959
such as the dreaded Chaos Insurgency or the
radical Serpent’s Hand, who obviously lack

00:01:40.959 --> 00:01:46.179
the capabilities to take to the stars and
make contact with SCP-179.

00:01:46.179 --> 00:01:51.149
Though we can imagine that if the day a hostile
third party Group of Interest gets their hands

00:01:51.149 --> 00:01:56.520
on spacefaring technology capable of reaching
SCP-179 ever comes, the Foundation would try

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:01.859
everything in its power to protect the anomaly
from any harm coming to it.

00:02:01.859 --> 00:02:07.829
As you’ll see, SCP-179 is incredibly important,
not just to the Foundation, but for the continued

00:02:07.829 --> 00:02:10.649
survival of mankind on the planet Earth.

00:02:10.649 --> 00:02:14.900
But let’s talk about what SCP-179 is, first.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:20.980
Floating in space, SCP-179 is a humanoid entity
with the appearance of an adult female, with

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:26.409
a matte black skin tone covering her body,
and long, flowing hair colored in the same

00:02:26.409 --> 00:02:27.409
substance.

00:02:27.409 --> 00:02:32.810
Ornate, golden symbols or tattoos decorate
SCP-179’s figure, some representing the

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:37.769
medieval alchemical symbols for the sun and
the six innermost planets.

00:02:37.769 --> 00:02:43.540
These include the symbol for gold on SCP-179’s
forehead, a symbol for mercury between her

00:02:43.540 --> 00:02:49.700
lips, one for copper located near her clavicles,
and corresponding symbols for iron, tin, and

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:52.610
lead, all placed down the length of her torso.

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:57.470
The entirety of her body reflects sunlight,
shining so brightly that it was her illuminated

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:03.060
figure appearing in orbital analysis instruments
that made Foundation astrophysicists aware

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:06.519
of Sauelsuesor’s existence in the year 1940.

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:12.930
Immediately, research into what SCP-179 was,
and what the anomaly was capable of began,

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:18.090
and the results showed, as her figure suggested,
that Sauelsuesor was intelligent and could

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.700
understand human language.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:25.829
To date, only one successful communication
attempt was made with SCP-179, but the results

00:03:25.829 --> 00:03:30.659
of that endeavor have been classified and
sealed away behind a memetic kill agent.

00:03:30.659 --> 00:03:36.689
But more on that later, we still need to discuss
what makes SCP-179 so special, y’know, besides

00:03:36.689 --> 00:03:41.650
being a shiny, floating, space-woman who calls
the scorching 10,000 degrees fahrenheit heat

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:43.689
of the sun her home.

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:49.540
While SCP-179 is located close to the sun,
it does not orbit it, and instead seems to

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:52.980
maintain a continuous orbit around the galaxy
itself.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:56.079
She’s really the center of the universe,
huh.

00:03:56.079 --> 00:04:00.900
Still, SCP-179 maintains a tangible connection
to our big, blue planet.

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:05.749
Most of the time, either like a watchful protector
or a curious observer, Sauelsuesor does not

00:04:05.749 --> 00:04:07.959
remove her gaze from the earth.

00:04:07.959 --> 00:04:09.439
And for good reason, too.

00:04:09.439 --> 00:04:13.659
She’s keeping our best interests in mind
by watching out for anything in the solar

00:04:13.659 --> 00:04:15.779
system that could bring us harm.

00:04:15.779 --> 00:04:18.579
Sauelsuesor is the lookout, essentially.

00:04:18.579 --> 00:04:23.170
Her movements are specifically related to
the coming of extraterrestrial threats, both

00:04:23.170 --> 00:04:28.060
anomalous and ordinary, which she signals
by pointing in their direction with one of

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:31.539
her arms, and making a series of signals with
her fingers.

00:04:31.539 --> 00:04:36.180
Whether these finger movements carry any specific
meaning, such as acting as a way to describe

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:40.380
information related to the danger, is as of
yet unknown.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:45.580
If more than one threat is incoming, SCP-179
has been observed to generate as many limbs

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:50.010
as it needs to make sure every potential danger
is noted and signaled.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:55.630
The nature of the things SCP-179 points at
are specifically objects on a collision course

00:04:55.630 --> 00:04:57.139
for earth.

00:04:57.139 --> 00:05:02.460
Sometimes they’re only asteroids, but on
occasion, SCP-179 has predicted the coming

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:07.750
of several high-security SCP objects before
they made their way to earth.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:13.800
It seems SCP-179 has a pretty decent radar
on negotiating what it defines as a threat,

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:18.430
too, as its warning signs are yet to be proven
wrong or exaggerated.

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:23.990
If SCP-179 starts pointing, the Foundation
knows it better start listening.

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:29.210
In some instances, SCP-179 detected threats
before any other party on earth had become

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:34.360
aware of them, and in others, before anyone
realized said objects were threats.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:39.699
This pinpoint accurate warning system indicates
that SCP-179 might know a lot more about the

00:05:39.699 --> 00:05:44.270
nature of the universe than what a first glance
would suggest.

00:05:44.270 --> 00:05:50.930
This ability to ascertain danger levels has
proven SCP-179 as a useful asset to the Foundation,

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:55.520
allowing them to prepare accordingly for the
impact of incoming extraterrestrial objects

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:57.460
that may be obstacles.

00:05:57.460 --> 00:06:01.569
After all, having a warning system that can
accurately signal the arrival of potential

00:06:01.569 --> 00:06:07.729
XK-Class end-of-the-world scenarios from space
is an incredible boon to the Foundation, specifically

00:06:07.729 --> 00:06:11.979
to the COEWS project, the Composite Orbital
Early Warning System.

00:06:11.979 --> 00:06:17.720
COEWS acts as a highly classified coalition
of Foundation sites, personnel, and even some

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:22.759
anomalies themselves, that monitor space for
objects and anomalies of interest.

00:06:22.759 --> 00:06:24.110
Sound familiar?

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:27.780
Thanks to SCP-179, these guys have their work
cut out for them.

00:06:27.780 --> 00:06:32.009
We bet if you looked inside the COEWS offices,
they’d be playing ping pong and watching

00:06:32.009 --> 00:06:38.760
movies the entire time, with a probe observing
SCP-179 set to trigger an alarm in case anything

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:39.760
happens.

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:41.550
Foundation budget dollars at work!

00:06:41.550 --> 00:06:43.510
But back to SCP-179.

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:49.419
It was Sauelsuesor’s movements that predicted
the arrival of several classified SCP objects,

00:06:49.419 --> 00:06:53.449
as well as general space debris, such as incoming
asteroids.

00:06:53.449 --> 00:06:57.370
While this didn’t mitigate the outcome of
the object’s collisions on earth, which

00:06:57.370 --> 00:07:02.260
sometimes resulted in heavy collateral damage
and civilian casualties that the Foundation

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:07.349
had to discreetly cover up, it did allow the
Foundation to plan their course of action

00:07:07.349 --> 00:07:11.240
for when the objects arrived in an organized
fashion.

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:17.000
SCP-179 even responded accurately to a Foundation
test intended to grab its attention, in which

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:22.990
an armed Type-11 Dimensional Weapon was fired
from Area-08, and was identified by Sauelsuesor

00:07:22.990 --> 00:07:28.130
when the shot reached 3,670 kilometers above
the planet’s surface.

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:33.860
All of SCP-179’s movements have been recorded
and logged by the Foundation in hopes of understanding

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:37.909
the anomaly’s intentions, motivations, and
accuracy.

00:07:37.909 --> 00:07:42.860
And it checks out, because the benevolent
SCP-179 has been nothing but helpful to the

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:43.860
Foundation.

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:48.759
Sure, she acts as the bearer of bad news for
horrible, potentially disastrous events, but

00:07:48.759 --> 00:07:51.300
the Foundation is never going to shoot the
messenger.

00:07:51.300 --> 00:07:56.360
They’ll just shoot the giant space demon
that wants to feed on earth’s minerals instead.

00:07:56.360 --> 00:08:00.310
And thanks to Sauelsuesor, they’ll have
enough time to prepare firepower the size

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:04.509
of a country’s combined ammunition and a
nice, comfy containment chamber for said space

00:08:04.509 --> 00:08:05.820
demon as well!

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:10.870
But most importantly, who is SCP-179 signaling
to?

00:08:10.870 --> 00:08:16.810
On 10/16/2003, the SCP Foundation decided
to find out for themselves.

00:08:16.810 --> 00:08:22.790
The event was monumental and resulted in SCP-179’s
object class being upgraded after contact

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:26.069
with the entity revealed new information to
the Foundation.

00:08:26.069 --> 00:08:30.630
On top of the security class upgrade, level
4 personnel working on research pertaining

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:35.640
to SCP-179 received promotions to higher clearances
as well.

00:08:35.640 --> 00:08:38.450
Hopefully that came with a decent pay increase!

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:43.440
Unfortunately for the reassigned personnel,
they were given a high dosage of Class-D amnestics,

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:45.800
with a 10 year retrograde effect.

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:48.650
No memories of the beautiful solar protector
for them.

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:54.540
But let’s focus here: what exactly happened
when the Foundation made contact with SCP-179

00:08:54.540 --> 00:08:56.920
that warranted this upgrade in security?

00:08:56.920 --> 00:09:00.700
The answer is only hidden behind a deadly
memetic kill agent.

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:06.670
A specially designed probe equipped with recording
devices and microsatellite features, but most

00:09:06.670 --> 00:09:12.170
importantly, capable of reaching SCP-179’s
solar position, was launched towards the anomaly.

00:09:12.170 --> 00:09:18.270
Initially, the Foundation classified SCP-179
as safe, but upon further exploration of the

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:23.500
entity’s purpose and behaviors, upgraded
that object class to the high-security classification

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:31.080
of thaumiel, meaning that SCP-179 is an anomaly
being used to contain other anomalies.

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:37.360
On the surface, SCP-179 may seem like just
another lunar anomaly, inoffensive and relatively

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:42.470
detached from anything of great importance,
but upon accessing the file’s top-secret

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:47.740
level-5 classifications, Sauelsuesor’s true
purpose becomes revealed.

00:09:47.740 --> 00:09:53.000
When contact between the probe and SCP-179
was established, the entity communicated with

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.250
the Foundation for the first time.

00:09:55.250 --> 00:10:00.960
She spoke in French, and introduced herself
as Sauelsuesor, and “the lookout”.

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:05.670
She asked the probe if it liked her brother,
apparently referring to the sun.

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:10.070
Upon establishing radio communications with
the entity, the Foundation asked Sauelsuesor

00:10:10.070 --> 00:10:14.620
who she reported to, as they recognized the
significance of her movements.

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:22.450
SCP-179 responded, saying she reported “To
those who know where to look.

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:23.450
To you.

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:26.030
To those who want to look.

00:10:26.030 --> 00:10:27.340
Not just you.

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:29.840
But you, too.”

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:35.510
When asked about her brother, the sun, Sauelsuesor
referred to the star as “Sauel”, saying,

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:38.620
“He warms me up.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:42.400
He is caring fire and loving light.

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:48.600
He caresses me with his arcs and his voice
and renews me.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:52.470
He is the source of all true light.

00:10:52.470 --> 00:10:54.640
He is your source.”

00:10:54.640 --> 00:11:00.320
The Foundation continued to probe more information
from SCP-179, learning that she was once a

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:05.630
child from earth, but would not disclose any
more information, such as how she reached

00:11:05.630 --> 00:11:09.390
her current position or gained her anomalous
abilities.

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:15.380
The reason for her secrecy being her desire
to remain free from “belonging” to any

00:11:15.380 --> 00:11:16.380
one person.

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:22.040
But the Foundation could not understand, they
had to try to pry more secrets from SCP-179’s

00:11:22.040 --> 00:11:27.500
mind, not just about incoming threats, but
about everything she knew.

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:31.490
Surely, she could see the benefit in protecting
the earth even further.

00:11:31.490 --> 00:11:36.180
Perhaps realizing the Foundation’s sometimes
unscrupulous morals and constant need for

00:11:36.180 --> 00:11:38.780
assimilation, Sauelsuesor refused.

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:44.380
Instead, she stated: “I am too big, and
you are too small.

00:11:44.380 --> 00:11:49.520
There is a sea of nothing and islands of light.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:51.610
I am their shore.

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:54.800
To you come the monsters.

00:11:54.800 --> 00:11:58.320
The pounding fists of void.

00:11:58.320 --> 00:12:02.450
The longing gods beyond our knowledge.

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:05.550
I am the lookout.

00:12:05.550 --> 00:12:08.870
I see the ripples in their wake.

00:12:08.870 --> 00:12:17.890
You want me to pledge my sight-know to you,
only to you, so you, only you, can be greater.

00:12:17.890 --> 00:12:23.660
Even if you find, restrain, defend.

00:12:23.660 --> 00:12:25.750
You want me to be yours.

00:12:25.750 --> 00:12:29.500
That is not why I am here.

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:31.530
There are others.

00:12:31.530 --> 00:12:33.940
Others I assist.

00:12:33.940 --> 00:12:36.020
Others I warn.

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:42.160
Others beyond your thin walls of grey, dry
paste-rock.

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:46.810
Others beyond the reach of your weary satellites.

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:50.910
Others beyond the home, our home.

00:12:50.910 --> 00:12:52.950
Others I know.

00:12:52.950 --> 00:12:55.420
Others I love.

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:58.020
Others you won't care for.

00:12:58.020 --> 00:13:00.770
Others that came before.

00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:11.820
And, over all, others beyond the little walls
of rules and bone and laws and flesh and memories

00:13:11.820 --> 00:13:18.640
and oaths you build around yourselves until
you don't even remember them.

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:20.650
Others I love.

00:13:20.650 --> 00:13:21.650
Dearly.

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:26.970
And yet, only my brother is equal to me.”

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:32.100
Immediately, the Foundation attempted to pry
further, asking Sauelsuesor who the ‘other’s

00:13:32.100 --> 00:13:33.580
she spoke of were.

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:38.570
But following her speech, Sauelsuesor only
smiled, and stated that she had no more words

00:13:38.570 --> 00:13:42.800
to say before ceasing communication entirely.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:46.990
Since that date, she has yet to respond to
any other messages or attempts to communicate

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:50.250
from the Foundation and any other groups of
interest.

00:13:50.250 --> 00:13:55.100
While the Foundation did not fully gain access
to the secrets and hidden knowledge that Sauelsuesor

00:13:55.100 --> 00:14:00.800
surely possesses, they can sleep safely knowing
that they have the galaxy’s best and literal

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:04.760
brightest security alarm they could possibly
ask for.

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:09.080
Now go check out “SCP-096 - Look at a Picture
of Shy Guy in Space?

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:14.460
The Shy Guy Questions and Theories (SCP Animation)”
and “NASA Lies?

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:19.880
SCP-2001 - Space Oddity (SCP Animation)”
for more space SCPs!

